---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Retry and failed-cone recovery — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-sky">For DevOps</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Retry and failed-cone recovery</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                Same authorization as Retry: DevOps, Project admin, Team-admin inherit, Platform admin. Developer is 403.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>Two layers</h2>
            <p>
                <strong class="text-foreground">In-run retry</strong> stays on the same
                step execution: running → retry_waiting → queued, with backoff
                <code class="text-foreground">delay = backoff × multiplier^(attempt-1)</code>,
                capped at 900 seconds. Default <code class="text-foreground">retry_max_attempts = 1</code>
                means off. Writes are default-unsafe for auto-retry; extracts and artifact-sql
                are default-safe. Unsafe blocks in-run auto-retry only.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong class="text-foreground">Failed-cone</strong> is a new run that still
                <em>plans</em> the full graph, skips <em>execution</em> of source succeeded
                nodes, and rebinds artifacts. It is not a trigger-time subgraph and not
                “run from step X”. Full retry remains the UI/API default (<code class="text-foreground">mode=full</code>).
                There is no auto-cone when in-run attempts exhaust — a human chooses full vs cone.
            </p>

            <h2>Policy snapshot</h2>
            <p>
                Pipeline defaults, optional step override, copied onto step executions at
                plan create (same snapshot pattern as agent-pool assignment). Publish
                freezes version defaults. Dual-path: legacy serial uses an inner loop in
                the serial engine; cone requires DAG execution (and artifact/DuckDB flags
                when those handlers are in the cone). No extra feature flag.
            </p>

            <h2>Abandon</h2>
            <p>
                Grace first. Then retry_waiting only if attempts remain,
                retry_on_abandoned is true, and the step is not unsafe. Otherwise terminal
                abandoned.
            </p>

            <h2>Artifacts across runs</h2>
            <p>
                Cone clones artifact rows into the new run. Resolvers never search other
                runs. Clones copy sensitivity and retention from the source. Audit payload
                has mode and counts, not URIs or secrets. Retry stays project-scoped.
            </p>

            <h2>Where to click</h2>
            <p>
                Preview the cone, then Retry / RetryRun, from run details or the schedule
                run list. Run History index and the visualizer do not expose the button.
                Missing project returns JSON 400 (not a login challenge) for the AJAX preview.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
